WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:02.580
 Filmmaking is a disease,
and you have to be sick.

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:04.129
And I'm super sick.

00:00:04.129 --> 00:00:05.127
[LAUGHING]

00:00:05.127 --> 00:00:07.622
[NON-ENGLISH MUSIC]

00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:21.010
The first thing that I would
tell an aspiring filmmaker

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:22.600
is to educate yourself.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:26.980
Be permeable to what is
around you with humility,

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.680
with respect, and
with also, an ability

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:33.520
to see yourself in that world
so that that world trusts you.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:34.160
That's key.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:41.960
I want to do this MasterClass
to demystify the process.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.750
Welcome to the workshop
of the "Queen of Katwe."

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:48.830
We are doing one scene to
show how to direct actors.

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:52.610
Actors look for the
ability to trust.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:56.090
Your work as a director
is to create a space where

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:58.760
they are allowed to bloom.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:00.920
When I'm budgeting
the picture, I'm

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:03.830
not going to let
people see my struggle.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.980
My formula is that every scene
has to do more than one thing.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:09.140
Every scene has to
do three things.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:11.300
Films under the guise
of entertainment

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:15.210
should open windows
in your heart.

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:17.700
Nothing is more
powerful than seeing

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:21.480
your own language, your
own color, your own people,

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:25.620
your own dramas on screen.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:30.020
If you don't tell your own
story, no one else will.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:32.880
I'm Mira Nair, and
this is my MasterClass.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:35.330
[MUSIC PLAYING]

